    "text": {
     "en": "The Middle Ages in Europe followed the fall of Rome. A system called feudalism arose, with kings giving land to lords, who gave land to knights, who protected peasants called serfs. The Church had great power.\nThe Crusades were holy wars between Christians and Muslims over Jerusalem. Trade and towns grew again, and guilds of merchants and craftsmen formed. In the east, Islam spread and the Arab world became a centre of learning in science and mathematics.\nLater the Black Death killed many people and weakened feudalism. New universities, such as Bologna and Oxford, appeared."
    }
